      "rev_n_2_a9b895_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_a9b895_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_a9b895",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error occurs because we're not updating the `friend_index` correctly after moving it to the top of the round. Let's modify our approach to handle this case more effectively.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_a9b895_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_afae1da671",
        "created_at": 1794530505.058072
      },
      "rev_n_1_255a02_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_255a02_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_255a02",
        "thought_text": "I understand the issue now. The current approach doesn't correctly handle the case where your friend needs to be the strongest boxer in the final stage. Let's modify the approach to ensure your friend always wins, regardless of their strength in the final stage.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_255a02_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_595333d058",
        "created_at": 1794530537.268011
      },
      "rev_n_3_2794af_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_2794af_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_2794af",
        "thought_text": "The error in the code is in the loop condition for calculating the cost to bribe opponents. It should be iterating over the number of groups your friend will advance to, not the number of groups in the current round. This oversight causes the function to incorrectly calculate the total cost when your friend is not the strongest boxer.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_2794af_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_4d0e730bed",
        "created_at": 1794530574.5618057
      },
      "rev_n_4_88c23b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_88c23b_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_88c23b",
        "thought_text": "Consider the optimal pairing strategy for each round",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2383849225683257357",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530595.509644
      },
      "rev_n_5_76dd7f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_76dd7f_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_76dd7f",
        "thought_text": "Pay attention to the position of your friend throughout the tournament",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2383849225683257357",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530595.5096614
      },
      "rev_n_6_02f845_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_02f845_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_02f845",
        "thought_text": "Minimize the number of rounds where your friend is not in the first position",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2383849225683257357",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530595.5096707
      },
      "rev_n_4_88c23b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_88c23b_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_88c23b",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error occurs because we're not updating the `friend_index` correctly after moving it to the top of the round. Let's modify our approach to handle this case more effectively by always considering the position of your friend relative to the advancing boxers in each round.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2383849225683257357",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_88c23b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_16eab15bc6",
        "created_at": 1794530617.0576468
      },
      "rev_n_7_ab1f1a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_ab1f1a_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_ab1f1a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach fails because it doesn't consider the possibility of your friend winning even if they're not the strongest in the final stage. We need to modify the strategy to ensure your friend always wins regardless of their strength.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235997245477191853",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530644.166937
      },
      "rev_n_8_935c58_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_935c58_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_935c58",
        "thought_text": "Instead of focusing on making your friend the strongest, we should focus on making sure they're the only contender in the final stage. This will guarantee they win regardless of their strength.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235997245477191853",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530644.1669528
      },
      "rev_n_9_b3320c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_b3320c_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_b3320c",
        "thought_text": "We can achieve this by always placing your friend in the first position of the final stage and only allowing stronger opponents to be in the second position. This way, your friend will always win the final match.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235997245477191853",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530644.1669607
      },
      "rev_n_7_ab1f1a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_ab1f1a_1",
        "node_id": "n_7_ab1f1a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach fails because it doesn't consider the possibility of your friend winning even if they're not the strongest in the final stage. We need to modify the strategy to ensure your friend always wins regardless of their strength by always placing them in the first half of the pairs at each stage, even if it means bribing other boxers.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235997245477191853",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_7_ab1f1a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_584bfbf00f",
